{
  "description": "std-slide-deck — generic presentation atom. An ordered list of slide nodes (`config.slides`, any render tree or @trait) shown one at a time, with a previous/next arrow on either side, a dot strip and a k / n counter underneath, and keyboard stepping through the host's KEY router (`config.nextKeys` / `config.prevKeys`, captured per `config.keymap`). The cursor clamps at either end unless `loop` is on. Each visit mounts the slide fresh, so its own entry animations replay. Carries no content or visual style: a realization supplies the slides and restyles via `bodyContent`. The default body picks the slide inside a mapped-children lambda, which expands static slides only; a deck whose slides hold stateful traits (forms, live lists) overrides `bodyContent` with one `presence` per slide gated on `@entity.slideIndex`. Every move emits SLIDE_CHANGED for speaker notes, timers or analytics.",
  "ledger": {
    "entries": {
      "ent_01M39MPG8EZJMEW9YAGD6SNM0W": {
        "bakedName": "SlideDeck",
        "curName": "SlideDeck",
